{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/779615-vampires-against-out-of-context-problems-in-your-games","id":779615,"title":"Vampires against Out-of-Context Problems in Your Games","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-04T01:25:21-08:00","id":779615,"title":"Vampires against Out-of-Context Problems in Your Games","content":"Ghosts. Spirits. Angels. Spider monsters. Rat horrors. Werewolves. Whatever it may be, how have you used or encountered supernatural threats from outside the world of vampires in your <b>Vampire: The Requiem </b>games? Did your characters persevere? Did they fail miserably, meeting Final Death or perhaps worse? How did their perspectives change as a result of these encounters? Did it awaken a curiosity, or a new drive to master the night's mysteries? Or did your character retreat into the world of the Kindred, thankful to go oblivious to the other things that lurk in the dark?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T02:37:37-08:00","id":779636,"title":"","content":"I had a Cabal of Tremere work together with a Strix (long story), one of the Tremere had it out for a player character, but since he had barely any sympathetic connection nor a Sympathetic Name it was not easy to find the PC. The PC meanwhile knew a sorcerer had it out for him, which led him to do some favours for an Elder Mekhet to clue him in about willworkers. A close call later, the help of the local Bishop was recruited to find the Tremere's hiding spot through good ol' Theban Sorcery. The coterie attacked and killed one member of the Cabal when they arrived and then prepared an ambush for when the other two returned. Being a surprised Mage is suffering.<br /> <br /> Afterwards, the PC in question stayed a sort of apprentice to the Mekhet and pick up what scraps of occult lore the Elder was willing to drop. The rest of the coterie were more like &quot;Fuck this!&quot; and got back to the night-to-night of the Danse Macabre.<br /> <br /> PS: Player characters swearing Oaths of Action within the Coterie is a really nice boost when you need to make something dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T04:46:03-08:00","id":779703,"title":"","content":"In my latest game, we're running a 2e vamp/wolf/mage/ling crossover. So far, all the PCs are vampires, but we've had the other supernaturals be noticable floating around. I've also played upon the whole Predator's Aura ability to sense werewolves, and extended it to the witches and wizards of the setting. So, its not -quite- an out of context problem for the vampires, since we're talking about a notice-on-sight reaction here. Changelings, with their Mask and lack of aura, however, are much more sneaky, though rumors and stories persist. Anyways, the point is that its not quite an out-of-context issue since vamps are aware of the other supernaturals, and have forged agreements, niches, and methods of dealing with each other. And, as physical beings, its not hard to know how to deal with them - mind control and sucking them dry always works. <br /> <br /> I introduced a Beshilu once, and the responce was to flee after it broke into other rats, though the group Gangrel mentioned that they were getting swarm form to eat them the next time, swarm-on-swarm action. <br /> <br /> Spirits and the like I haven't really used. I'm of the opinion that Vampire isn't really meant to deal with ephemeral beings without additional rules, so I don't quite bring it up. I've introduced ghosts a few times, but each time it was rather a flop. The Mehket Ordo had the playtest Coil with a few psychic abilities to let them play, but the others... just didn't -care- about the ephemeral entites. I was told that it was a vampire game, and that we had characters that wanted to do vampiric things. Running a shamanistic or mage-y story wasn't something the group was interersted in.<br /> <br /> I've slid in several references to angels and ghosts and the Underworld into the game. But again, it wasn't any kind of story that the players were interested in running. So, we meandered over to variations on other vamp stories. <br /> <br /> So, I guess the answer to your question is &quot;ask not to have out of context stories.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T08:52:45-08:00","id":779847,"title":"","content":"I usually incorporate the rest of the World of Darkness into things, but the most common folks vampire characters run into are werewolves. The Big Two sort of have similar priorities in concerns of territory and often butt heads, which can lead to pretty nasty antagonism but also powerful alliances.<br /> <br /> Usually at least one pack gets the spotlight, often one closest to the territory of the characters and, rather than play it safe or try to avoid them, they've usually gone out to try and ensure there was an understanding between the coterie and pack. The end result is either an agreement to not interfere in other people's business, which has fallen apart and led to trouble, or a more tight 'you scratch our backs, we'll scratch yours' arrangement. In our last game it got so the players incorporated werewolves into their plans and one of them made an effort to kill the Prince-appointed liaison to the werewolves and take it's place. There was a lot of roadblocks, namely the vampires who thought the coterie had something to do with the previous liaison's demise, the winning over of packs beyond the one that shared their territory, initiation into a pack and a duel with the other vampire trying to take the title, who was on good terms with the coterie and had helped them before.<br /> <br /> So in the end I'd say they really take advantage of the opportunities afforded by the presence of werewolves, but I want to make it clear that it wasn't easy or safe for them, they weren't a wolf among sheep like when the coterie dealt with mortals, they're a wolf among wolves. In one game a vampire allowed a pack to stay at their haven, and after they sort of abused the ghouls realized he had bitten off more than he could chew, because they weren't going to leave.<br /> <br /> Other out of context problems tend to be seen as unique things more than part of a larger culture. The Centimani who is willing to pay out for that strange object the players stole, a demon they want something from before they release him, a Claimed that happened to be preying on things in their territory. Shards of the World of Darkness. I think the opening up of the World of Darkness beyond their principality has really encouraged some exploration. Not always but it's there. Our last game ended on a very dramatic cliffhanger and the players have made it clear afterwards their characters would leave the territory to find answers and power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T12:34:56-08:00","id":780049,"title":"","content":"On meeting the local solitary werewolf, the PCs in my most recent game withdrew to a polite distance very quickly. And maintained a polite distance when he strolled into Elysium to discuss something with the city's leading vampires. And were very polite when they asked him for help. This was probably influenced by two of the most active players being long-time WOD fans and knowing cWOD werewolves in particular - the assumption that they'd be hostile and dangerous.<br /> <br /> They were more intrigued by the ghosts they encountered, at least until they started to attack one of them...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T12:39:24-08:00","id":780057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Craig Oxbrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/779615-vampires-against-out-of-context-problems-in-your-games?p=780049#post780049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were more intrigued by the ghosts they encountered, at least until they started to attack one of them...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh that reminds me, we had a powerful vampire ghost in our last game as well, who was in turn controlled by a powerful ghost-witch. After the first couple encounters the players were very wary of engaging with the problem again in any direct fashion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T19:57:04-08:00","id":780329,"title":"","content":"I am still waiting for a pc to kill someone by feeding so they can become a ghosts anchor and figure out what to do with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T14:44:09-08:00","id":780720,"title":"","content":"I'd like to use the <i>Beshilu </i>against vampires in a game sometime. Start with outbreaks of disease, maybe in one of the more rundown feeding grounds\u2014though a rat infestation in more upscale neighborhoods and a sudden outbreak do provide an interesting contrast. Exterminators, ghouled doctors, they won't be equipped to deal with something like the Rat Hosts. Vampires may be immune but they can become carriers. Eventually, the vampires are going to have to send someone (read: the player characters) to investigate. Imagine rotting basement walls, skittering beneath the floor, the scent of diseased blood from victims torn to pieces and hauled down under the floorboards. Swarms of rats with golden eyes and an eerie intelligence haunt the vampires' steps, resisting Animalism commands. Peel away the rotten panels and you might discover a bulbous, man-sized rat-thing amid a crawling mass of shrieking rodents, their chittering maws frothing with poison. Take a wrong step to escape and you might find yourself moving into a darkened world you don't recognize. Gibbering masses of toxin float among the rats, pulsating like boils ready to burst.<br /> <br /> If you don't deal with the problem, you might find more unwanted guests, like Lupines howling outside your door. Or maybe the vampires must make a deal with a local pack, if one exists, lest the Gauntlet fray so much a Wound is born.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T15:05:18-08:00","id":780729,"title":"","content":"I threw an unfettered Geist at my players once. It was being controlled by a Dragolescu. They kept finding Twilight Network codes everywhere, left by its former Sin-Eater, who the vampire had driven mad so he could steal the Geist as a slave (as I recall; it's been awhile).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T18:32:49-08:00","id":785676,"title":"","content":"Does a Morbus blood cult of apocalyptic leanings creating a nearly city-wide blood magic infused zombie outbreak counts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T04:53:59-08:00","id":785898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/779615-vampires-against-out-of-context-problems-in-your-games?p=785676#post785676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a Morbus blood cult of apocalyptic leanings creating a nearly city-wide blood magic infused zombie outbreak counts?</div> </div> </div> </div> Not really. Zombie outbreak is part of the vampire toolbox already. See larvae (Night Horrors) and draugr (gangrel clan book). You're doing it differently, but same concept applies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T07:38:03-08:00","id":785963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/779615-vampires-against-out-of-context-problems-in-your-games?p=785898#post785898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not really. Zombie outbreak is part of the vampire toolbox already. See larvae (Night Horrors) and draugr (gangrel clan book). You're doing it differently, but same concept applies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not different at all, i do admit - just checking on how fresh are people on the zombie = larvae thing. They were pretty much larvae &quot;mass-produced&quot; with a mix of Blood Magic &amp; Cachexy, to get a convenient number of &quot;Typhoid Joes &amp; Janes&quot; ready and in place to jumpstart <b>tamed</b> larvae packs in a quick and at the same time stealthy manner. When their presence in the city and &quot;witch hunt&quot; were exposed they threw discretion through the window, swarmed a subway car and went zombie outbreak mode in bus-subway-train nexus at the rush hour. Almost a third of the kindred in the city (Rio de Janeiro) met with final death while trying to contain (or escape from) the mess and the Masquerade was stretched ridiculously thin with lots of media manipulation about riots, gang &amp; militia warfare, and if it held out was possibly only because a state of emergency had been declared two nights before and much of the movement in parts of the city already controlled or restricted. The Uratha joined in the late part of the mop-up, but it was something of a last minute cavalry arrival thing and so took far less of a beating. Fun times. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Beside this, have toyed a bunch with the Reaper spirits and Red Jack (who in my games is the particularly cunning and evolved Ba of a Mekhet he torpored himself for safety reasons and a number of &quot;disciples&quot; in Ars Speculorum that he uses as surrogate anchors) from Mythologies, Mnemovores (in the same game, kindred that had their post-torpor &quot;changed souls&quot; repossessed by Reapers and fill the void with memories in place of vitae), and the Kanaima from Skinchangers, who in the game have a sort of rivalry with the strix and also spawned kindred and other beings from time to time.<br /> <br /> The Reapers in particular may become more of an issue as the mass creation - and destruction - of dozens of kindred and hundreds, maybe thousands, of blood-magic tainted larvae in a single night has left something of a spiritual mark in the area, something of a problem in a city that already has centuries-old &quot;fractures&quot; in its peculiar geomancy and the final death of the local Hierophant, that also happened to be the kindred most knowledgeable in the subject and who kept a lid on these things. A bloody trickle has opened in some tunnels in the area and in time it may become a river... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-04-2022, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T09:08:27-08:00","id":786014,"title":"","content":"Honestly, more vampire games need more zombie outbreaks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T03:23:20-08:00","id":786610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/779615-vampires-against-out-of-context-problems-in-your-games?p=786014#post786014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, more vampire games need more zombie outbreaks.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, true. My version of the Legio Mortuum for games in Camarilla times would frequently figure with a number of them on leash as attack hounds. Legionaries sent away from the Home Necropolis to support the breathing legions - basically coteries of &quot;honored ancestors&quot; playing sword-&amp;-sandal undead black ops units, with the duty of neutralizing supernatural threats to their lving countrymen - frequently made whole packs of them out of barbarians or rebels confronted in the provinces or borders of the Republic or Empire.<br /> <br /> Glen Cook's Black Company series of books was a major influence in the portrayal of these &quot;tutelary units&quot; of the roman legions in distant fronts, for loads of gonzo entertainment of the group. Also loads of <a href=\"http://www.eldritchdark.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Clark Ashton Smith</a> - but then i use concepts and imagery from his works with almost anything that can pass for non-contemporary fantasy. Beside this i also inserted a few cameos, as both adversary and ally of convenience, of the Cheiron Group, a far-reaching and well-connected merchant house harkening back to Seleucid times at least. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Have also something of a weak spot for stuff from Wicked Dead and toyed with variants of my own, like other creepie-crawlies beside the Strix generating strange lost brands of blood-drinking or flesh-eating undead, among other stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-04-2022, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}